{"parentUuid":"059d27c6-e118-4c7d-bf0c-d83359c1e944","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgY1FVHxNA32uJyQhLvqc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2A.5: DONE\n\nCommit `10435e1` on `phase-2a-archive` is pushed, and the PR waits for the 2A gate. Full details are in `step-2A.5.md` in the notes folder.\n\n**Crop check: 48 of 50 candidates pass (96%, 95% interval 86.5–98.9%).** The 50 picks are one per year, spread across 1770–1964, from 45 batches with no more than 2 from any one.\n- **Fail, #21 (1862 *Daily dispatch*):** AmericanStories gives the article a stray first box. It's the last line of the letter above (\"To Hon. W. H. Seward … Franklin Pierce\"), and the article's OCR doesn't contain it.\n- **Fail, #50 (1964 *Arizona tribune*):** no crop. The scan has no batch path, and loc.gov has no item for that issue, so no IIIF service can be named.\n- **Saved by a new fallback:** two pages, from 1796 and 1845, returned 404 because LoC has reissued their batches (ver01 is now ver02). The fallback asks loc.gov for the page's current service, and with it both pass.\n\n**Display-headline precision, from 200 dropped lines judged by hand:**\n- **First rule: 71.0% (64.4–76.8%).** It dropped dates that belong to the article, like \"Out Ghosts Next / Monday Evening\".\n- **Final rule: 97.5% (94.3–98.9%)**, on a fresh sample of 200. Masthead lines are now dropped only while they lead the headline, and short titles must stand alone as words (that fixes *PoStry* and *VIOLA*).\n\n**Test runs during the read:** 05:29–05:49 UTC, all light, and the read kept its usual speed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1066,"cache_read_input_tokens":754118,"output_tokens":589,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1066,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":589,"cache_read_input_tokens":754118,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1066},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"34483d53-9751-46b9-abcd-33dea0b84bb8","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgY1FUHvPxap7KAbhUwZ9","requestRef":"84600054-39b0-4ca6-8a06-a32599139f6c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"d5ca3503-886c-485c-9ee0-f65f61ab6a36","timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:11:40.976Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-archive","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
