{"parentUuid":"5d06a61d-bd69-454a-8442-1ec5c314f0bf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f40c2187-e8b4-47d5-9c53-ee1f5c6e6ab4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UVkvSFRdLQTbvhe6TMPntF","type":"tool_result","content":"Crop per box, cache the crops, and show headlines without their mastheads\n\n- crop_urls makes one IIIF crop per box, in bbox_list order, which is\n  the reading order. The single crop over every box (decision 18) took\n  in the columns between them.\n- Requests to the Library of Congress go at most one a second, name the\n  project, and are retried while the server is busy. Crops are cached\n  under data/crops/ by URL, and a reissued batch (ver01 to ver02) is\n  found through loc.gov.\n- display_headline drops the masthead lines that lead a headline, and\n  the OCR is untouched. On 200 drops judged by hand, precision went from\n  71.0% to 97.5% (95% interval 94.3-98.9%) with the rule change.\n- The crop check: 48 of 50 candidates pass\n  (eval/results/phase2a/crop-check.md).\n- The skeleton shows its three crops and its display headline.\n- Decision 26.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M65TB339Z3PRN9NE59VN84HW\n\nRead the whole archive: 180 years, kill test 1, and decision 25\n\n- All 180 year files at revision 77e27fa6, 340.4 GB, in 118.6 min, an\n  aggregate 47.8 MB/s. Every manifest's bytes_read equals the listed\n  size, no year failed, and no partial file was left.\n- 370,313,913 articles gave 1,050,459 candidates. Outputs take 1.94 GB,\n  and the highest peak memory was 535 MB (1910).\n- Kill test 1 (eval/results/phase2a/kill-test-1.md): the worker's\n  process group was SIGKILLed with 1881-1884 in flight. The 96 finished\n  manifests stayed byte-identical, and the four ran again as attempt 2","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e6bc3e2e-451a-47a1-9cd3-08be130c2365","timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:45:19.085Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Crop per box, cache the crops, and show headlines without their mastheads\n\n- crop_urls makes one IIIF crop per box, in bbox_list order, which is\n  the reading order. The single crop over every box (decision 18) took\n  in the columns between them.\n- Requests to the Library of Congress go at most one a second, name the\n  project, and are retried while the server is busy. Crops are cached\n  under data/crops/ by URL, and a reissued batch (ver01 to ver02) is\n  found through loc.gov.\n- display_headline drops the masthead lines that lead a headline, and\n  the OCR is untouched. On 200 drops judged by hand, precision went from\n  71.0% to 97.5% (95% interval 94.3-98.9%) with the rule change.\n- The crop check: 48 of 50 candidates pass\n  (eval/results/phase2a/crop-check.md).\n- The skeleton shows its three crops and its display headline.\n- Decision 26.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M65TB339Z3PRN9NE59VN84HW\n\nRead the whole archive: 180 years, kill test 1, and decision 25\n\n- All 180 year files at revision 77e27fa6, 340.4 GB, in 118.6 min, an\n  aggregate 47.8 MB/s. Every manifest's bytes_read equals the listed\n  size, no year failed, and no partial file was left.\n- 370,313,913 articles gave 1,050,459 candidates. Outputs take 1.94 GB,\n  and the highest peak memory was 535 MB (1910).\n- Kill test 1 (eval/results/phase2a/kill-test-1.md): the worker's\n  process group was SIGKILLed with 1881-1884 in flight. The 96 finished\n  manifests stayed byte-identical, and the four ran again as attempt 2","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b93375fe-7090-4dad-828e-a50ee8e25dad","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2a-archive","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":23,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_n