{"parentUuid":"3bcadef4-1449-422b-8e3f-a8150e392749","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgY5cv9yuHJJiUrv9MZLP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2A.5 follow-ups: DONE. Commit `9d56340` is pushed, with decisions 28 and 29. Full notes are in `step-2A.5-follow-ups.md`.\n\n**Headline rule, on the same 200 judged lines:**\n- 0 of the 5 mis-drops remain.\n- 37 of the 195 correct drops are lost: 22 bare issue numbers, 5 Whole No. lines, 7 datelines that don't match the record's date, and 3 junk lines.\n- All 158 lines it still drops are correct (95% interval 97.6–100%).\n- Across all candidates it drops 7,509 lines, down from 10,287, and every one was dropped by the old rule too.\n- One reading call: a weekday that matches the issue settles a dateline whose digits OCR misread. Requiring every digit to match would lose 17 more correct drops and save no mis-drop.\n\n**Missing scans:** 335,907 candidates (32.0%) have no batch path; the counts by year are in `eval_a.json`. But 92.4% of them sit on reels whose batch other pages name, so only 25,595 need loc.gov.\n\n**My mistake:** a probe broke loc.gov's 20-requests-a-minute JSON limit, so this machine is blocked until about 05:03. `crops.get` now spaces those requests 3.5 s apart.\n\nCrop 21 is recorded as a known limitation.\n\n**Question:** should 2B build the reel-to-batch map?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":829,"cache_read_input_tokens":371349,"output_tokens":489,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":829,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":489,"cache_read_input_tokens":371349,"cache_creation_input_tokens":829,"cache_creation":{"ephem