ort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-archive","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"1b28da52-a68b-45a2-91b8-67dfe4c8e4ee","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"efbe7dae-4a3a-47ef-9f27-91c90fdaed9c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S1nb7yvHgiDzBdQtRudhgq","type":"tool_result","content":"## Crop check: 48 of 50 pass (96%, 95% Wilson interval 86.5–98.9%)\n\n`eval/results/phase2a/crop-check.md` has a verdict and a reason for each pick. The contact sheet is `crop-check-1.jpg` to `crop-check-5.jpg`, and the picks are in `crop-check.json`.\n\n- **Picks:** one per year, from 50 years evenly spread over the 173 years with candidates (1770–1964), drawn at random with a per-year fixed seed. They come from 45 LoC batches, with at most 2 from any one, and have 105 boxes in all.\n- **Pass means:** the crops, one per box in `bbox_list` order, show the article's OCR text from its first line, in reading order, with nothing missing.\n- **Failures:**\n  - **#21, 1862 Daily dispatch:** box 1 is the last line of the item above, a letter's address and signature (\"To Hon. W. H. Seward … Franklin Pierce\"). The article's OCR doesn't contain it, so AmericanStories gave the article a stray box.\n  - **#50, 1964 Arizona tribune:** there is no crop. The scan has no batch path, and loc.gov lists the title (Phoenix, 1958–197?) but has no item for 1964-11-06, so no IIIF service can be named.\n- **Saved by the reissued-batch fallback:** #2 (1796) and #16 (1845) are recorded in `ver01` batches that tile.loc.gov no longer serves (404), and loc.gov lists them under `ver02`. Without the fallback, 4 picks would have failed.\n- **Notes on passes**, all of them with the crop matching the OCR:\n  - Overlapping boxes repeat a line in 7 picks.\n  - Box edges clip a first or last letter as the OCR does in 5.\n  - 3 articles start mid-story, where AmericanStories split them.\n  - In 3, a box runs into the next item.\n  - Box 1 is the paper's own dateline in #15, an ornament in #2, and a sliver of the item above in #33.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4f5ea8ed-3de0-4063-899a-79c7804655dc","timestamp":"2026-10-30T14:19:29.774Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Crop check: 48 of 50 pass (96%, 95% Wilson interval 86.5–98.9%)\n\n`eval/results/phase2a/crop-check.md` has a verdict and a reason for each pick. The contact sheet is `crop-check-1.jpg` to `crop-check-5.jpg`, and the picks are in `crop-check.json`.\n\n- **Picks:** one per year, from 50 years evenly spread over the 173 years with candidates (1770–1964), drawn at random with a per-year fixed seed. They come from 45 LoC batches, with at most 2 from any one, and have 105 boxes in all.\n- **Pass means:** the crops, one per box in `bbox_list` order, show the article's OCR text from its first line, in reading order, with nothing missing.\n- **Failures:**\n  - **#21, 1862 Daily dispatch:** box 1 is the last line of the item above, a letter's address and signature (\"To Hon. W. H. Seward … Franklin Pierce\"). The article's OCR doesn't contain it, so AmericanStories gave the article a stray box.\n  - **#50, 1964 Arizona tribune:** there is no crop. The scan has no batch path, and loc.gov lists the title (Phoenix, 1958–197?) but has no item for 1964-11-06, so no IIIF service can be named.\n- **Saved by the reissued-batch fallback:** #2 (1796) and #16 (1845) are recorded in `ver01` batches that tile.loc.gov no longer serves (404), and loc.gov lists them under `ver02`. Without the fallback, 4 picks would have failed.\n- **Notes on passes**, all of them with the crop matching the OCR:\n  - Overlapping boxes repeat a line in 7 picks.\n  - Box edges clip a first or last letter as the OCR does in 5.\n  - 3 articles start mid-story, where AmericanStories split them.\n  - In 3, a box runs into the next item.\n  - Box 1 is the paper's own dateline in #15, an ornament in #2, and a sliver of the item above in #33.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"53755c0d-8334-4ad8-8420-be2839beb1a1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2a-archive","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":6,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1b28da52-a68b-45a2-91b8-67dfe4c8e4ee","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-archive","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
