upon looking for driver. found that individual by the roadside-the jug evidently master OF him\n538\t\n539\t=== c-104 | 1889-02-11 | Morning journal and courier. | 685 words | flags: spiritual\n540\tHEADLINE: FAITH AND OBEDIENCE.\n541\tOPENING: The Example of the Great Master Prayer as a Source of Comfort and Strength-The Lesson of Obedience Discourse by Rev. I. M. Foster at St. John Street M. K. Church. Rev. Mr. Foster preached forcible sermon yesterday morning at the St. John street M. E. church. It was full of thought. He said that his subject was \"Boisterous Pillows and Contrary Winds,\" and not Boisterous, Bilious and Contrary Minds\" as had be\n542\tWINDOW: example in his retirement and com munion with God as one full of suggestion and comfort to the Christian. Herein was to be found the key to obtaining spiritual solace and strength in hours of temptation, grief, afiction and weakness. The second fact to be gained from the text is obedience to Chris\n543\t\n544\t=== c-105 | 1958-06-15 | Diario las Américas. | 229 words | flags: supernatural\n545\tHEADLINE: e. ANGLlcIsMo EN- ESPANoL /  /  / -coNTEMpoRANEo\n546\tOPENING: Con eli prop6sto de contdbuir al mantenimieuto IL IA Uuresa d nueNro dioma diariamente pubHcaremos Ell esa pagna in ardculo del tntereante y novedoso Diccionario de Angicismos del eminents tntrna. SUPRA Hasta la 15@ edicion de su diccionaro 1925 la Academia no habia cataogado este prefijo. En- la 16a aparecen definidas unica mente dos voces en- cuya composition entra esta partcula ' Sc hacs referencia a otras dos\n547\tWINDOW: s de setnta. Supra denda endma de, arriba, mas ALA, encarecimiento y 50 presta a la formation de vocablos tan TITLES como suprarrenaI, supra dichO, supernatural Con frecuencia Sc encuentran hermosos y ex presivos neologismos compuestos con este prefijo, y de SUI utnidad dan mueara los sguiente lug\n548\t\n549\t=== c-106 | 1859-03-21 | The daily exchange. [volume] (Baltimore, Md.) 1858-1861 | 172 words | flags: spirit, spirits\n550\tHEADLINE: \n551\tOPENING: GENERAL WILLIAM I. HASKELL, the we'll known Tennessee orator and politician, died at the Hop knsville, Kentucky, Insane Asylum, on Sunday last. The Cincinnati Commercial says: He was at one time one of the most brilliant men of the South He was one of the first orators of the nation poet by nature and the author of some beautiful stanzas and gallant soldier distinguished in the Mexican war. His insanity is believ\n552\tWINDOW: tiful stanzas and gallant soldier distinguished in the Mexican war. His insanity is believed to be chargeable to the effect of an excessive of ardent spirits upon highly excitable nervous system. The country was first informed of bis insanity about two wears ago. He was confined for time in the Kent\n553\tWINDOW: th says: His dearest friends regret that the bal my hand of death has at length relieved him from suffering. The grave never closed over more gallant spirit; affection can never weep over a more loveable, high. toned and chyalrie man.\n554\t\n555\t=== c-107 | 1916-03-15 | Norwich bulletin. | 623 words | flags: witch\n556\tHEADLINE: HOW ADJUTANT GENERAL / WOULD ASSEMBLE FORCES /  / II State Troops Are Called Out-Ni- / antic Would Be Mobilization Point.\n557\tOPENING: In the Connecticut cavalry troops are called out for work on the Mex lean border, General Cole SAYS the point of mobilization would be Man tic. At present only about eighty horses are at the disposal of the two Connecticut troops, but the government has for some time. | said General Cole. had a reduisiton for other horses in the state. | and it could easily supply with horses the rest of the wa strength squadron of\n558\tWINDOW: giments OF infantry, one regiment Of calvary, six batteries OF field artillery lex Guiding the four Yale batteries), thres companies of signal troops witch 1873 men. and sanitary troops numberins 395. II its peace organizaton the Fifth division has no engineers, and a battalion would have to be form\n559\t\n56