{"parentUuid":"a1d10352-d0bf-4a1e-b41a-fd655c93437d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"efbe7dae-4a3a-47ef-9f27-91c90fdaed9c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013mt3hEFDSTRtkU8SYPnF9C","type":"tool_result","content":"Eval A: the EDA, what the candidates are, and the lexicon's recall\n\n- make eval (scripts/eval_a.py) writes eval/results/eval_a.json and\n  eight charts to eval/results/eval_a/ in 41 s. The samples are seeded,\n  and a rerun keeps the judgments made by hand.\n- EDA: counts by year, by state (11.2% of candidates have no state) and\n  by term; lengths (median 358 words); OCR quality (median 92.7% of\n  words in the dictionary); and reprint clusters, which leave 801,071\n  distinct stories from 1,050,459 candidates. 20 of 20 sampled cluster\n  pairs are the same story.\n- Composition: 7 of 200 candidates are ghost reports (3.5%, 95%\n  interval 1.7-7.0%), about 36,800 candidates or 22,300 stories. The\n  rest are figurative, fiction, names and titles, religious, social\n  events and other, with 15 OCR accidents among them.\n- Recall: none of 300 near-miss articles and none of 300 non-candidates\n  is a ghost report, so at most 1.26% of each pool. No misses means no\n  lexicon v2.\n- wilson() moves to paperghosts/stats.py. The bar charts size their\n  margin from their labels and give a zero bar a tooltip, and an axis\n  under one gets a step under one.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"70b2bbba-513f-49df-8cfd-7d3295e08a45","timestamp":"2026-10-30T14:33:20.077Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Eval A: the EDA, what the candidates are, and the lexicon's recall\n\n- make eval (scripts/eval_a.py) writes eval/results/eval_a.json and\n  eight charts to eval/results/eval_a/ in 41 s. The samples are seeded,\n  and a rerun keeps the judgments made by hand.\n- EDA: counts by year, by state (11.2% of candidates have no state) and\n  by term; lengths (median 358 words); OCR quality (median 92.7% of\n  words in the dictionary); and reprint clusters, which leave 801,071\n  distinct stories from 1,050,459 candidates. 20 of 20 sampled cluster\n  pairs are the same story.\n- Composition: 7 of 200 candidates are ghost reports (3.5%, 95%\n  interval 1.7-7.0%), about 36,800 candidates or 22,300 stories. The\n  rest are figurative, fiction, names and titles, religious, social\n  events and other, with 15 OCR accidents among them.\n- Recall: none of 300 near-miss articles and none of 300 non-candidates\n  is a ghost report, so at most 1.26% of each pool. No misses means no\n  lexicon v2.\n- wilson() moves to paperghosts/stats.py. The bar charts size their\n  margin from their labels and give a zero bar a tooltip, and an axis\n  under one gets a step under one.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"848f27b2-3de5-448f-98c1-57d8aa5500da","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2a-archive","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":9,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a1d10352-d0bf-4a1e-b41a-fd655c93437d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5