{"parentUuid":"83c302b2-e888-4f11-9b2b-869e0c90d2ec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYazHqRFysB1EJSnd95m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013Dmq85oSYpckitTa96anwH","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && gh pr create --base main --head phase-2a-archive --title \"Phase 2A: archive read and EDA\" --body-file - <<'EOF' 2>&1 | grep -v -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\"\nPhase 2A of `Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md`: the archive read and EDA.\n\n- Lexicon v1 with OCR variants, the near-miss lexicon, and a prefilter that samples each pool 2,000 articles a year (decisions 19–21)\n- `IngestArchiveWorkflow` and `make ingest`: a fresh process per year, a pinned dataset revision, and a year skipped only while every output's hash matches (decisions 22–24)\n- The full read: all 180 year files, 340.4 GB in 118.6 min, giving 370,313,913 articles and 1,050,459 candidates (decision 25). Kill test 1 ran during it.\n- Crops, one per box and cached, and the display headline without its masthead lines (decisions 26 and 28). The crop check passes 48 of 50.\n- Eval A (`make eval`, 42 s), with eight charts (decisions 27, 29 and 30):\n  - the EDA\n  - what the candidates are: 3.5% are ghost reports\n  - reprint clusters\n  - scans with no batch path\n  - the lexicon's recall\n- Recall: a flag-word screen of 38,600 more non-candidates found 4 ghost reports. So lexicon v1 finds about 49% of the reports, and at least 27%. Lexicon v2 is proposed in decision 30 and has not been run.\n- `Docs/RESUME.md` gets the Phase 2A STATUS block, and `Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md` gets new items for 2B and 2C.\n\n## Phase 2A gate (run at `36e20e3`)\n\n- [x] All 180 years are done and none failed. Six ran twice, each with its reason (decision 25).\n- [x] Disk use is reported: the outputs take 1.94 GB, and 39 GiB are free.\n- [x] `make ingest YEARS=1850` reproduces 1850: all three outputs are byte-identical, with the committed manifest's sha256.\n- [x] Kill-test evidence: `eval/results/phase2a/kill-test-1.md` and its three Temporal UI screenshots.\n- [x] Both crop-check failures are explained: #21 has a stray box and #50 has no loc.gov item.\n- [x] The EM's spot check of 20 random candidates and 10 random non-candidates (seed \"EM spot-check 2A\") is cited in the STATUS block.\n- [x] `make lint` exits 0, and `make test` passes 160 tests.\n- [ ] Prefilter recall: misses were found, so the plan calls for lexicon v2 and a re-run. Decision 30 proposes v2, and it waits on the EM.\n- [ ] CI is green (it runs on this PR).\n\nOpen for the EM: lexicon v2. The choice is between merging this as it stands and running v2 as its own step, or holding the PR until v2 is done.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF","description":"Open the Phase 2A pull request into main"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1389,"cache_read_input_tokens":376189,"output_tokens":2735,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1525},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1389,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2735,"cache_read_input_tokens":376189,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1389,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1389},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013Dmq85oSYpckitTa96anwH":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && gh pr create --base main --head phase-2a-archive --title \"Phase 2A: archive read and EDA\" --body-file - <<'EOF' 2>&1 | grep -v -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\"\nPhase 2A of `Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md`: the archive read and EDA.\n\n- Lexicon v1 with OCR variants, the near-miss lexicon, and a prefilter that samples each pool 2,000 articles a year (decisions 19–21)\n- `IngestArchiveWorkflow` and `make ingest`: a fresh process per year, a pinned dataset revision, and a year skipped only while every output's hash matches (decisions 22–24)\n- The full read: all 180 year files, 340.4 GB in 118.6 min, giving 370,313,913 articles and 1,050,459 candidates (decision 25). Kill test 1 ran during it.\n- Crops, one per box and cached, and the display headline without its masthead lines (decisions 26 and 28). The crop check passes 48 of 50.\n- Eval A (`make eval`, 42 s), with eight charts (decisions 27, 29 and 30):\n  - the EDA\n  - what the candidates are: 3.5% are ghost reports\n  - reprint clusters\n  - scans with no batch path\n  - the lexicon's recall\n- Recall: a flag-word screen of 38,600 more non-candidates found 4 ghost reports. So lexicon v1 finds about 49% of the reports, and at least 27%. Lexicon v2 is proposed in decision 30 and has not been run.\n- `Docs/RESUME.md` gets the Phase 2A STATUS block, and `Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md` gets new items for 2B and 2C.\n\n## Phase 2A gate (run at `36e20e3`)\n\n- [x] All 180 years are done and none failed. Six ran twice, each with its reason (decision 25).\n- [x] Disk use is reported: the outputs take 1.94 GB, and 39 GiB are free.\n- [x] `make ingest YEARS=1850` reproduces 1850: all three outputs are byte-identical, with the committed manifest's sha256.\n- [x] Kill-test evidence: `eval/results/phase2a/kill-test-1.md` and its three Temporal UI screenshots.\n- [x] Both crop-check failures are explained: #21 has a stray box and #50 has no loc.gov item.\n- [x] The EM's spot check of 20 random candidates and 10 random non-candidates (seed \"EM spot-check 2A\") is cited in the STATUS block.\n- [x] `make lint` exits 0, and `make test` passes 160 tests.\n- [ ] Prefilter recall: misses were found, so the plan calls for lexicon v2 and a re-run. Decision 30 proposes v2, and it waits on the EM.\n- [ ] CI is green (it runs on this PR).\n\nOpen for the EM: lexicon v2. The choice is between merging this as it stands and running v2 as its own step, or holding the PR until v2 is done.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF","description":"Open the Phase 2A pull request into main"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"040e7118-9527-45af-ba73-06bab46520cf","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgYazGnQqfhu7DcuzyQnY","requestRef":"67ae3fbe-0e91-4b68-a70f-f57806380af8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"superpowers:dispatching-parallel-agents","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"eb12c521-5bc6-4c53-b36e-8a45d9180114","timestamp":"2026-10-30T14:34:22.536Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-archive","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
