{"parentUuid":"f29e2ce6-bf8a-49f2-84f8-88ef1ab68ce1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYccVwYo86E53zYzewJG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good — all three deliberate breaks correctly fail the test, confirming the one-version check properly blocks v2 EDA until the read finishes (preventing mixed lexicon counts). While that completes, I'll draft the brief for reviewers of the 200 added candidates per the 2A.7 protocol.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1474,"cache_read_input_tokens":498262,"output_tokens":4092,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2709},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1474,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4092,"cache_read_input_tokens":498262,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1474,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1474},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"5ad87bf6-6081-49b0-9085-9a8878ac413b","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgYccUr5VKkfnnwYejdMj","requestRef":"ad75aa79-04e0-4a33-a6d3-0d8d258b10b8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e164f2a6-46ac-4ce8-a320-aece438528f4","timestamp":"2026-10-30T14:55:48.439Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-lexicon-v2","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"e164f2a6-46ac-4ce8-a320-aece438528f4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYccVwYo86E53zYzewJG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VwfWWTvYbybudYj5jCfLMn","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/added/brief.txt","content":"You are judging old newspaper articles for an evaluation of a ghost-report search over the Library of Congress's digitized American newspapers (1770s to 1960s). Every article in your batch was drawn at random from the articles that the search's new spiritualist terms made candidates, and that its older ghost words did not. Each holds at least one of: spiritualism or spiritualist(s); séance; a spirit phrase such as spirit world, spirit message, control of spirits, disembodied, or spirits of the dead; ouija or planchette; or the words spirit and medium somewhere in one article. For each article, decide one thing: is it a ghost report?\n\nGHOST REPORT, the only positive: a ghost, haunting, apparition or spirit manifestation, told as something that happened or was claimed to. These all count when told as real or as claimed, in news, a letter, court testimony or an anecdote told as true: spirit-rapping, table-tipping, materializations, a spirit speaking through a medium or a ouija board, spirit photographs, a séance described as having happened with its phenomena, a house where noises or lights are taken for the dead, a sighting of a dead person. A particular séance or manifestation exposed as a fraud still counts, because it was claimed, just as a ghost scare that turns out to be a trapped man counts.\n\nNOT a report:\n- fiction: stories, serials, poems, jokes and allegories, even ones about spirits\n- a séance, spiritualist meeting or lecture only announced or advertised for later\n- spiritualism discussed in general, for or against: essays, sermons, editorials, a lecture's arguments, mediums' tricks explained in general, a list of a church's meetings\n- an advertisement for a medium's or clairvoyant's services\n- a witch or witchcraft with no ghost; devils and demons, which are religious\n- spirit as mood, courage, liquor or the Holy Spirit; \"the spirit of\" anything; a medium of exchange, an artist's medium, a medium size\n\nMark CLOSE when:\n- it might be a report on a fuller reading, for example a window mentions a séance's phenomena but is cut off\n- it tells of a hallucination, a delusion, an insane person's visions, a claim of spirit control (for example in a court defence), a felt presence of the dead, or a dream or premonition of the dead (the project hasn't settled these yet)\n- you are unsure for any other reason\n\nThe text is OCR of old newspapers and is often garbled; read through the noise. Each article is a block:\n\n=== <id> | <date> | <paper> | <length> | terms: <the new terms that made it a candidate>\nHEADLINE: ...\nOPENING: the first ~420 characters of the article\nWINDOW: ~300 characters around a word of those terms (up to 6 windows)\n\nYour batch is BATCH_PATH, with N_ITEMS articles (ids FIRST_ID to LAST_ID). Read every block yourself. Read the file with the Read tool, in parts with offset and limit if it is long, until you reach the end.\n\nWrite your verdicts to OUT_PATH as a JSON list with one object per article, in file order:\n{\"id\": \"FIRST_ID\", \"verdict\": \"no\", \"note\": \"\"}\nverdict is \"no\", \"close\" or \"report\". The note is required for close and report: one sentence on what the article says happened and why it is or might be a report. For \"no\", leave it empty, or give a few words if it was near.\n\nUse only the batch file. Don't read other files, search the web, or write code that decides verdicts (keyword rules would defeat the purpose). You may run one short script at the end only to check that your output is valid JSON with exactly one verdict for every id.\n\nReply with the count of each verdict and every id you marked close or report, with its note. Nothing else.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1474,"cache_read_input_tokens":498262,"output_tokens":4092,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2709},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1474,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4092,"cache_read_input_tokens":498262,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1474,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1474},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VwfWWTvYbybudYj5jCfLMn":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/added/brief.txt","content":"You are judging old newspaper articles for an evaluation of a ghost-report search over the Library of Congress's digitized American newspapers (1770s to 1960s). Every article in your batch was drawn at random from the articles that the search's new spiritualist terms made candidates, and that its older ghost words did not. Each holds at least one of: spiritualism or spiritualist(s); séance; a spirit phrase such as spirit world, spirit message, control of spirits, disembodied, or spirits of the dead; ouija or planchette; or the words spirit and medium somewhere in one article. For each article, decide one thing: is it a ghost report?\n\nGHOST REPORT, the only positive: a ghost, haunting, apparition or spirit manifestation, told as something that happened or was claimed to. These all count when told as real or as claimed, in news, a letter, court testimony or an anecdote told as true: spirit-rapping, table-tipping, materializations, a spirit speaking through a medium or a ouija board, spirit photographs, a séance described as having happened with its phenomena, a house where noises or lights are taken for the dead, a sighting of a dead person. A particular séance or manifestation exposed as a fraud still counts, because it was claimed, just as a ghost scare that turns out to be a trapped man counts.\n\nNOT a report:\n- fiction: stories, serials, poems, jokes and allegories, even ones about spirits\n- a séance, spiritualist meeting or lecture only announced or advertised for later\n- spiritualism discussed in general, for or against: essays, sermons, editorials, a lecture's arguments, mediums' tricks explained in general, a list of a church's meetings\n- an advertisement for a medium's or clairvoyant's services\n- a witch or witchcraft with no ghost; devils and demons, which are religious\n- spirit as mood, courage, liquor or the Holy Spirit; \"the spirit of\" anything; a medium of exchange, an artist's medium, a medium size\n\nMark CLOSE when:\n- it might be a report on a fuller reading, for example a window mentions a séance's phenomena but is cut off\n- it tells of a hallucination, a delusion, an insane person's visions, a claim of spirit control (for example in a court defence), a felt presence of the dead, or a dream or premonition of the dead (the project hasn't settled these yet)\n- you are unsure for any other reason\n\nThe text is OCR of old newspapers and is often garbled; read through the noise. Each article is a block:\n\n=== <id> | <date> | <paper> | <length> | terms: <the new terms that made it a candidate>\nHEADLINE: ...\nOPENING: the first ~420 characters of the article\nWINDOW: ~300 characters around a word of those terms (up to 6 windows)\n\nYour batch is BATCH_PATH, with N_ITEMS articles (ids FIRST_ID to LAST_ID). Read every block yourself. Read the file with the Read tool, in parts with offset and limit if it is long, until you reach the end.\n\nWrite your verdicts to OUT_PATH as a JSON list with one object per article, in file order:\n{\"id\": \"FIRST_ID\", \"verdict\": \"no\", \"note\": \"\"}\nverdict is \"no\", \"close\" or \"report\". The note is required for close and report: one sentence on what the article says happened and why it is or might be a report. For \"no\", leave it empty, or give a few words if it was near.\n\nUse only the batch file. Don't read other files, search the web, or write code that decides verdicts (keyword rules would defeat the purpose). You may run one short script at the end only to check that your output is valid JSON with exactly one verdict for every id.\n\nReply with the count of each verdict and every id you marked close or report, with its note. Nothing else.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5ad87bf6-6081-49b0-9085-9a8878ac413b","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgYccUr5VKkfnnwYejdMj","requestRef":"ad75aa79-04e0-4a33-a6d3-0d8d258b10b8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a28c27d9-3fd8-4655-b16f-7090f730ed97","timestamp":"2026-10-30T14:55:57.569Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-lexicon-v2","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
