 The record-union. [volume] (Sacramento, Calif.) 1891-1903 | terms ['seance']\nHEADLINE: SLATER,s sEANCES. /  / He Gave His Ballot Tests to an APP /  /  / nreciative Audience.\nJohn Slater, the inimitable,\" gave another of his wonderful test seances last evening to an appreciative audi ence. Among other manifestations he gave the ballot test, or reading of sealed letters. He will repeat his seance tonight at Pythian Castle, Ninth and streets, at s o'clock. Mr.. Slater certainly hit off his answers last night to the satisfaction of his audience and most of his questioners, others being more or less embarrassed by his answers and illusions to tender subjects and episodes which elected much rilarity among the audience. In one instance a mother was told that her son, from whom she had not heard for eleven years, was not dead, but could be heard from by writing to a certain address in Melbourne, Australia. 1t is safe to say that if a letter to that address brings her a reply from her wandering boy, she will have full faith in future in the correctness Of Slater S tests. \n\n##### 3-034 | 1919-06-18 | Ellsworth American. [volume] (Ellsworth, Me.) 1855-current | terms ['ouija']\nHEADLINE: Motto for Dead Authors.\nWe are told that once, when Pa fence Worth was spelling out the end iess pages of the Sorry Tale\" she came TO sudden stop, then wrote, This be nuff,\" and knocked off for the night. A blessed phrase, and. Of a certainty, her finest inspiration. Would hat all dead authors would adopt 1t as heir motto; and with ouija boards, md table legs, and automatic pencils, write as their farewell message to the world those three short, comedy words, This be nuff.\"-Agnes Repplier. In Atlantic. \n\n##### 3-023 | 1920-07-19 | Alexandria gazette. [volume] (Alexandria, D.C.) 1834-1974 | terms ['spiritualism']\nHEADLINE: PREDICT THE ELECTION OF cox\nNew York. July l9.--lt has come! Owners Of astral bodies, Auras and the l!ke--;n other words spirits have gene into politics. According to Melvin A. Fogg, of the First Spiritualist Church, of Trenron y. j.. Abraham Lincoln has sent a message back to his mortal fellow countrymen that Governor James NJ. Cox will surely be elected in November. Not only that. but this message was received before Governor Cox had been nomirated--a week before the convention opened in San Francisco.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a1586478-36f2-4d24-b8fc-ed17b506f00b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2a-lexicon-v2","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":363,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":4},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"83516631-a6b7-4748-b104-e4c91a27d586","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-lexicon-v2","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
