{"parentUuid":"c73455c3-0355-4818-b6ad-b05dd2dc9b72","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4acd64b9-626e-4904-824b-5a9167cf4217","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dnsf2Tn5xDe5yJEufrUTRz","type":"tool_result","content":"36:- The Temporal dev server (`make temporal`, persisting under `data/temporal/`), a worker, and a smoke workflow with a heartbeat and a retry policy (`make smoke`).\n38:  - Tinker: credits, the base models available for LoRA training and sampling, and whether trained weights can be downloaded\n105:1. Write `POLICY.md`, build the gold set, freeze it and hash it.\n106:   - `POLICY.md` settles delusions and hallucinations with one rule. Eval A counts a 1904 defendant pointing at an \"imaginary\" spectre in court as a report, and a 1909 lunacy hearing's spooks as other. Its interval barely moves either way.\n112:6. LoRA training on Tinker, iterating on the dev split until improvements stop. Each iteration is recorded.\n113:7. Eval B, ablations B1 to B10, and edge-case slices E1 to E14.\n114:   - Eval B also has the reader screen the random reservoirs, for a recall bound that doesn't rest on flag words (decision 30). The Tinker credit check sets how many it reads.\n117:10. The full pass over all triaged candidates.\n228:- **Technical execution:** both kill tests, eval B with its intervals, and 100% verified quotes.\n230:- **Rules:** started and finished inside the window, prior work credited, tags `devchallenge` and `hf26challenge`.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d920501b-7e0a-4ec8-a8cb-141831a172c9","timestamp":"2026-10-30T17:07:06.828Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"36:- The Temporal dev server (`make temporal`, persisting under `data/temporal/`), a worker, and a smoke workflow with a heartbeat and a retry policy (`make smoke`).\n38:  - Tinker: credits, the base models available for LoRA training and sampling, and whether trained weights can be downloaded\n105:1. Write `POLICY.md`, build the gold set, freeze it and hash it.\n106:   - `POLICY.md` settles delusions and hallucinations with one rule. Eval A counts a 1904 defendant pointing at an \"imaginary\" spectre in court as a report, and a 1909 lunacy hearing's spooks as other. Its interval barely moves either way.\n112:6. LoRA training on Tinker, iterating on the dev split until improvements stop. Each iteration is recorded.\n113:7. Eval B, ablations B1 to B10, and edge-case slices E1 to E14.\n114:   - Eval B also has the reader screen the random reservoirs, for a recall bound that doesn't rest on flag words (decision 30). The Tinker credit check sets how many it reads.\n117:10. The full pass over all triaged candidates.\n228:- **Technical execution:** both kill tests, eval B with its intervals, and 100% verified quotes.\n230:- **Rules:** started and finished inside the window, prior work credited, tags `devchallenge` and `hf26challenge`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e69c36ec-e02b-4e2d-b793-891503adba38","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2a-lexicon-v2","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":363,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":4},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c73455c3-0355-4818-b6ad-b05dd2dc9b72","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},