{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","hash":"8e56d556dfde897e5ce4162c3e5cbd1d11a8abf6171aa3442eee7d6515484f89","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now `RESUME.md`: the next step, and the Phase 2A STATUS block updated with the v2 numbers and the in-sample caveat."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014XVVTKd2UoUuKtcnfeB1AT","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/RESUME.md","old_string":"**Phase 2B: schemas and data layer** (`BUILD-PLAN.md` section 4), once PR #2 is merged. Lexicon v2 (decision 30) waits on the EM. If it is accepted, its re-read runs before anything is loaded into Atlas.","new_string":"**Phase 2B: schemas and data layer** (`BUILD-PLAN.md` section 4), once PR #3 (lexicon v2) is merged. Whether to drop the ouija rule is the EM's call (decision 31). Dropping it takes a filter on `terms`, not a re-read."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X9D7qQgVzsxBh4DXmByUcj","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/RESUME.md","old_string":"## STATUS: Phase 2A, archive read and EDA (2026-10-30)\n\nBranch `phase-2a-archive`, PR #2.\n\nBuilt:\n- Lexicon v1, with OCR variants, and the near-miss lexicon (decisions 19–21). `IngestArchiveWorkflow` and `make ingest`, which skip a year only while every output's hash matches (decisions 22–24).\n- The full read of all 180 AmericanStories year files at revision `77e27fa6` (decision 25).\n- Crops, one per box, fetched once and cached, and the display headline without its masthead lines (decisions 26 and 28).\n- Eval A (`make eval`, 42 s, 4.0 GB at peak). It produces the EDA, the candidates' composition, the lexicon's recall and eight charts (decisions 27, 29 and 30).\n\nMeasured:\n- 370,313,913 articles in 16,887,460 pages, giving 1,050,459 candidates (2,837 per million) and 6,872,539 near-miss articles.\n- The read took 118.6 min for 340.4 GB, at 47.8 MB/s with four years at a time.\n- 3.5% of candidates are ghost reports (1.7–7.0%), about 36,800. Reprints put 31.4% of candidates in 80,770 clusters, which leaves 801,071 distinct stories.\n- Lexicon v1 finds about 49% of the ghost reports, and at least 27%. That rests on 4 reports found among 38,900 non-candidates (decision 30).\n- The crop check passes 48 of 50 (86.5–98.9%). The display headline drops 7,509 lines at 158 of 158 precision on the judged sample (97.6–100%).\n- 32.0% of candidates have no batch path, and 92.4% of those are on reels whose batch is known (decision 29).\n\nGate:\n- All 180 years are done, and none failed. Six ran twice: 1872 and 1889 lost their streams, and kill test 1 cost 1881–1884 their first attempts (decision 25).\n- Disk: the outputs take 1.94 GB (`data/candidates` 1.3 GB, `data/samples` 565 MB, counts 956 KB, manifests 720 KB), and 39 GiB are free.\n- `make ingest YEARS=1850` reproduces 1850. With its candidates moved aside, a rerun wrote all three outputs byte-identical, with the sha256 in the committed manifest.","new_string":"## STATUS: Phase 2A, archive read, EDA and lexicon v2 (2026-10-30)\n\nBranches `phase-2a-archive` (PR #2, merged) and `phase-2a-lexicon-v2` (PR #3, step 2A.8).\n\nBuilt:\n- Lexicon v1, with OCR variants, and the near-miss lexicon (decisions 19–21). `IngestArchiveWorkflow` and `make ingest`, which skip a year only while every output's hash matches (decisions 22–24).\n- Lexicon v2, which adds five spiritualist rules and records in each candidate's `terms` the rules that matched it (decision 31).\n- Two full reads of all 180 AmericanStories year files at revision `77e27fa6`:\n  - v1's (decision 25), now archived in `data/archive/lexicon-v1/`\n  - v2's (decision 31)\n- Crops, one per box, fetched once and cached, and the display headline without its masthead lines (decisions 26 and 28).\n- Eval A (`make eval`, 93 s, 4.7 GB at peak):\n  - It produces the EDA, the candidates' composition, the lexicon's recall and eight charts (decisions 27, 29 and 30).\n  - It then compares v2 with v1, and measures a judged sample of v2's added candidates (decision 31).\n  - `make eval-v1` reproduces v1's record from the archive.\n\nMeasured:\n- 370,313,913 articles in 16,887,460 pages. Lexicon v2 gives 1,236,122 candidates (3,338 per million) and 6,695,792 near-miss articles. v1 gave 1,050,459 (2,837 per million).\n- Each read takes about two hours for 340.4 GB, with four years at a time: 118.6 min for v1 and 120.6 min for v2.\n- Ghost reports: 3.5% of v1's candidates (1.7–7.0%), about 36,800, and 7.0% of the 185,663 that v2 adds (4.2–11.4%), about 13,000 more.\n- Reprints put 30.3% of v2's candidates in 91,301 clusters, which leaves 952,591 distinct stories.\n- Recall:\n  - Lexicon v1 finds about 49% of the ghost reports, and at least 27% (decision 30).\n  - Lexicon v2 finds about 84%, and at least 48%. **Both figures are in-sample:** v2's rules were chosen from the misses of the same screen.\n  - 2C's eval B gives the independent figure (decision 31).\n- The crop check passes 48 of 50 (86.5–98.9%). The display headline drops 7,509 lines at 158 of 158 precision on the judged sample (97.6–100%).\n- 32.0% of v2's candidates have no batch path, and 93.0% of those are on reels whose batch is known (decisions 29 and 31).\n\nGate:\n- All 180 years are done in both reads, and none failed.\n  - In v1's read, six ran twice: 1872 and 1889 lost their streams, and kill test 1 cost 1881–1884 their first attempts (decision 25).\n  - In v2's read, every year finished at the first attempt, all at code version `2d6ff0faaf81`.\n- v1 ⊆ v2: all 1,050,459 v1 candidates are still candidates, and none of the 185,663 added holds a v1 term.\n- Disk: the v1 archive and v2's outputs take 4.1 GB, within the 10 GB budget, and 36 GiB are free.\n  - `data/archive/lexicon-v1`: 1.8 GiB\n  - v2's `data/candidates`: 1.5 GiB\n  - v2's `data/samples`: 563 MiB\n- `make ingest YEARS=1850` reproduces 1850 under both lexicons. With its candidates moved aside, a rerun wrote all three outputs byte-identical, with the sha256 in the manifest.\n- `make eval-v1` reproduces eval A's v1 record byte for byte, apart from `generated_at`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xn3ohXzs159oPQtcAqs2f2","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/RESUME.md","old_string":"- The EM's spot check, seed \"EM spot-check 2A\", read 20 random candidates and 10 random non-candidates against their stored text:","new_string":"- The EM's spot check of v1, seed \"EM spot-check 2A\", read 20 random candidates and 10 random non-candidates against their stored text:"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QJok7D6S5WWYw9ZSYhhsqJ","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/RESUME.md","old_string":"- **Lexicon v2 is the EM's call** (decision 30). Spiritualist terms would add about 161,000 candidates (+15%) and catch 3 of the 4 missed reports. Adding them takes a full re-read: 118.6 min and 340.4 GB.\n- The recall estimate rests on 4 reports, 2 of them borderline. Its screen would still catch only 5 of eval A's 7 reports once their lexicon terms are masked.\n- `POLICY.md` (2C) has to settle delusions, hallucinations, spirit control and a felt presence of the dead.\n- 25,595 candidates need loc.gov to name their page's IIIF service, and its JSON API allows 20 requests a minute. 2B looks them up only for reports (decision 29).","new_string":"- **The ouija rule is flagged** (decision 31): none of its 6 sampled candidates is a report (0–39%). Dropping it is the EM's call, and a filter on `terms` would remove 5,124 candidates.\n- v2's 84% recall is in-sample. The screen behind both lexicons' recall rests on 4 reports, 2 of them borderline. Even with their lexicon terms masked, it would still catch only 5 of eval A's 7 reports.\n- v2's gain rests on 14 reports in 200, 2 of them borderline.\n- `POLICY.md` (2C) has to settle these cases:\n  - delusions and hallucinations\n  - spirit control and a felt presence of the dead\n  - decision 31's two borderline kinds\n- 27,817 of v2's candidates need loc.gov to name their page's IIIF service, and its JSON API allows 20 requests a minute. 2B looks them up only for reports (decision 29).\n- The reader's job is 1,236,122 candidates, 17.7% more than v1's. The Tinker credit check weighs that before the full pass."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
